docs/how-it-works.md:36:| `prepare-commit-msg` | Adds `Refs #<number>` to the message. The number is the first number in the branch name (`fix/123-login` gives `Refs #123`). The hook does nothing when the message already contains `#<number>`, or when git gives a commit source. Git gives a commit source for `git commit -m` and `-F`, templates, merges, squashes, and amends. Thus, the hook adds the reference only when git opens an editor for the message |
